-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_strings_err_multichar.pcpp - break step of lex_strings.pcpp:
  a character literal of several characters (PR0064, a warning: it is the
  int32 its bytes make, 'ab' = 97 * 256 + 98); past 4 characters it is too
  long for its type and keeps the last 4, still one report

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\lex_strings_err_multichar.pcpp -r
    pcpp res\tests\lex_strings_err_multichar.pcpp -r -t x86_64-linux-gnu   (runs in WSL)
  Each marked line reports that warning, once (the build reports nothing
  more about it), then the program prints:
  EXPECT:
    24930
    1650680933
    [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  EXITCODE: 0
  The [Heap] line is the debug build's heap report.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_strings_err_multichar;

begin
  println("{}", 'ab'); // WARN PR0064@17: character literal: multi-character character constant
  println("{}", 'abcde'); // WARN PR0064@17: character literal: character constant too long for its type
end.
